    <summary>radare2 is a scriptable set of tools and libraries for reverse engineering and forensics.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
radare2 is a scriptable set of tools and libraries for reverse engineering and forensics. It started as a command-line hexadecimal editor and grew into a complete framework for analysing, emulating, debugging, patching and disassembling binaries - from local files and kernel memory to remote gdb servers.

**What this package installs**

The official Windows build from the GitHub release, unpacked as a portable package. Every tool in the archive is on the `PATH` through Chocolatey's shims: `radare2` (also as `r2`), `rabin2`, `rasm2`, `rax2`, `rahash2`, `radiff2`, `rafind2`, `ragg2`, `rarun2`, `rasign2`, `rafs2`, `rapatch2`, `ravc2`, `r2agent`, `r2r` and the `r2pm` package manager. The install script picks the archive for the machine: 64-bit, 32-bit (also with `--x86`), or ARM64 on Windows on ARM.

**Plugins**

Most plugins ship with the stock install; more are available through `r2pm`, for example r2ghidra (the native Ghidra decompiler), r2frida, r2dec and esilsolve:

```
r2pm update
r2pm install r2ghidra
```

**Supported targets**

Architectures include x86/x86-64, ARM/AArch64, MIPS, PowerPC, SPARC, RISC-V, SuperH, m68k, AVR, Xtensa, WebAssembly, Java/Dalvik, MSIL and many more. File formats include ELF, Mach-O, PE/PE+, COFF, DEX, ART, Java class, WASM, Windows minidumps, BIOS/UEFI images, firmware and console ROMs, plus a range of filesystems.

**Documentation and community**

- The official radare2 book: https://book.rada.re
- Source and issue tracker: https://github.com/radareorg/radare2
- Chat: `#radare` on irc.libera.chat, Matrix `#radare:matrix.org`, Telegram https://t.me/radare, Discord https://discord.gg/MgEdxrMnqx
]]></description>
